WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.225
Double-free prevention in safe Rust comes
from ownership rules,

2
00:00:03.305 --> 00:00:05.831
but lifecycle-sensitive code still needs
tests and review.

3
00:00:05.911 --> 00:00:09.132
Tests should cover creation, ownership
transfer, cleanup, repeated calls,

4
00:00:09.212 --> 00:00:12.481
failed initialization, cancellation,
shutdown, and wrapper drop behavior.

5
00:00:12.561 --> 00:00:15.336
These are the paths where cleanup
assumptions are easiest to miss.

6
00:00:15.416 --> 00:00:17.348
Error-path testing is especially
important.

7
00:00:17.428 --> 00:00:19.112
If construction fails halfway through,

8
00:00:19.192 --> 00:00:21.818
which resources have been acquired and
which must be released?

9
00:00:21.898 --> 00:00:24.771
If shutdown is called before startup
completes, what is still owned?

10
00:00:24.851 --> 00:00:27.328
If an external API reports an error after
taking ownership,

11
00:00:27.408 --> 00:00:28.448
which side must clean up?

12
00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:31.550
Code review should focus on custom `Drop`,
unsafe blocks, raw pointers,

13
00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.603
FFI ownership transfer, allocator
assumptions, callback lifetimes,

14
00:00:34.683 --> 00:00:36.565
shared ownership, `Weak` upgrade behavior,

15
00:00:36.645 --> 00:00:39.123
and any path where cleanup can happen in
more than one place.

16
00:00:39.203 --> 00:00:42.819
Reviewers should ask whether exactly one
cleanup authority exists for each resource.

17
00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:46.367
Tooling concepts such as Miri and
sanitizers can support confidence near unsafe or

18
00:00:46.447 --> 00:00:46.843
FFI code.

19
00:00:46.923 --> 00:00:48.756
They do not replace a clear ownership
model,

20
00:00:48.836 --> 00:00:52.007
but they can help teams validate
assumptions around low-level boundaries.

21
00:00:52.087 --> 00:00:55.555
Dependency review also matters when
external crates provide wrappers over native

22
00:00:55.635 --> 00:00:56.130
resources.

23
00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:59.381
Regression tests should be added when
ownership and cleanup bugs are fixed.

24
00:00:59.461 --> 00:01:01.195
If a duplicate cleanup path was possible,

25
00:01:01.275 --> 00:01:03.504
capture the lifecycle edge in a test where
practical.

26
00:01:03.584 --> 00:01:07.250
Update safety contracts and API
documentation so future maintainers understand which

27
00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.420
path owns cleanup and why.
